A. Raw-Data-to-Review-Ready Analytics Copilot 
• Summary: Accelerate business decision-making by turning raw CSV/SQLite exports 
and ad-hoc questions into review-ready executive analysis and interactive charts in 
minutes. 
• Problem Description: Data scientists and analysts spend hours writing boilerplate 
exploratory scripts, cleaning messy columns, and formatting reports for non-technical 
stakeholders. Participants must build a self-correcting analytics copilot that ingests 
raw business data, runs natural-language queries via validated SQL/Python, and 
outputs a structured, review-ready analysis report with visuals. 
• Expected Functionalities: 
• CSV/SQLite uploader with automated schema inspection and data-quality 
health checks. 
• Natural-language query interface that generates and executes read-only 
SQL/Python code with automatic error self-correction. 
• Auto-rendered visual charts (bar, line, scatter) paired with statistical outlier 
callouts. 
• One-click exportable review-ready executive summary in Markdown/PDF 
format. 
• Suggested Data Requirements: A messy, multi-column raw CSV or SQLite database 
(~1,000 rows covering SaaS subscriptions, e-commerce orders, or customer churn with 
missing values and date irregularities). 
